IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`

-- The Convention, Chapters I and II: scope and definitions (Articles 1 and 2), documents of
-- carriage (Articles 3 to 9) and the rights of consignor and consignee (Articles 10 to 16),
-- with the documents part of Article 34.  Source: source/CAA1988.txt lines 257 to 505 (First
-- Schedule), 831 to 1113 (Second Schedule) and 1406 to 1663 (Third Schedule).
--
-- Every rule takes the Convention as its first input.  Where the three texts differ the rule
-- answers each separately; where a text has no such provision the rule is a REFUSE that says
-- so, never a figure or a yes/no taken from another text.
--
-- Where the three texts read alike, the rule does not take the Convention.

§ `Chapter I -- Scope: definitions`

§§ `Article 1. International carriage`

-- 1(2): "international carriage" means carriage in which, according to the agreement between
-- the parties, the places of departure and destination, whether or not there is a break or
-- a transhipment, are within the territories of two High Contracting Parties, or within the
-- territory of a single High Contracting Party if there is an agreed stopping place within
-- another State (First and Third Schedules) or within a territory subject to the sovereignty,
-- suzerainty, mandate or authority of another Power (Second Schedule).  The three wordings
-- give one test.

@ref "Convention, Article 1(2) (First, Second and Third Schedules)"
GIVEN f IS A `Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carriage is international carriage` IF
        f's `according to the agreement between the parties the places of departure and destination are within the territories of two High Contracting Parties`
     OR (    f's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party`
         AND f's `there is an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State or Power`)

@ref "Convention, Article 1(1)"
GIVEN f IS A `Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carriage is international carriage of persons, baggage or cargo by aircraft for reward` IF
        f's `the carriage is of persons, baggage or cargo`
    AND f's `the carriage is performed by aircraft`
    AND (   f's `the carriage is for reward`
         OR f's `the carriage is gratuitous carriage performed by an air transport undertaking`)
    AND `the carriage is international carriage` f

-- 1(3): carriage by several successive air carriers is one undivided carriage if the parties
-- regarded it as a single operation, whether under one contract or a series; it does not lose
-- its international character because one contract or a series is performed wholly within the
-- territory of one State.

@ref "Convention, Article 1(3)"
GIVEN s IS A `Successive Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carriage is one undivided carriage` IF
        s's `the carriage is to be performed by several successive air carriers`
    AND s's `the parties have regarded it as a single operation`

@ref "Convention, Article 1(3)"
GIVEN s IS A `Successive Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undivided carriage keeps its international character` IF
        `the carriage is one undivided carriage` s
    AND s's `one contract or a series of contracts is to be performed entirely within the territory of the same State`

§§ `Article 2 and Article 34. State and postal carriage; extraordinary circumstances`

-- 2(1): the Convention applies to carriage by the State or legally constituted public bodies
-- if within Article 1.  The Additional Protocol lets a High Contracting Party declare that it
-- does not apply to international carriage performed directly by the State.  2(2) (Second
-- Schedule): not to carriage under an international postal Convention; (First Schedule): not
-- to carriage of mail and postal packages; (Third Schedule) 2(2) and (3): the carrier is liable
-- only to the postal administration, and the Convention otherwise does not apply to postal items.
-- 34 (Second Schedule): the Convention does not apply to international carriage by experimental
-- trial nor to carriage in extraordinary circumstances outside the normal scope of an air
-- carrier's business.  34 (First Schedule: Articles 3 to 9; Third Schedule: Articles 3 to 8)
-- takes only the documentary provisions out of those cases.

@ref "Convention, Article 2(1), Article 2(2) and (3), Article 34 and the Additional Protocol"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention applies to the carriage` IF
        `the carriage is international carriage of persons, baggage or cargo by aircraft for reward` f
    AND NOT (    f's `the carriage is performed directly by the State`
             AND f's `the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol as to Article 2(1)`)
    AND NOT f's `the carriage is of mail and postal packages, or is performed under the terms of an international postal Convention`
    AND (CONSIDER c
         WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
                 NOT f's `the carriage is performed by way of experimental trial by air navigation undertakings with a view to the establishment of a regular line of air navigation`
             AND NOT f's `the carriage is performed in extraordinary circumstances outside the normal scope of an air carrier's business`
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN TRUE)

@ref "Convention, Article 34"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisions on documents of carriage apply to the carriage` IF
        `the Convention applies to the carriage` c f
    AND NOT f's `the carriage is performed in extraordinary circumstances outside the normal scope of an air carrier's business`

@ref "Convention, Article 2(2) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      f IS A `Carriage Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable only to the postal administration` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no provision that the carrier of postal items is liable only to the postal administration"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention (First Schedule) has no provision that the carrier of postal items is liable only to the postal administration"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            f's `the carriage is of mail and postal packages, or is performed under the terms of an international postal Convention`
        AND f's `the carriage is performed by aircraft`

§ `Chapter II -- Documents of carriage`

§§ `Section 1, Article 3. Passenger ticket`

-- 3(1): the contents.  Second Schedule: place and date of issue, places of departure and
-- destination, agreed stopping places, name and address of the carrier, and a statement that
-- the carriage is subject to the Convention's liability rules.  First and Third Schedules:
-- an indication of the places of departure and destination; an indication of at least one
-- stopping place where both places are in one High Contracting Party's territory with an
-- agreed stopping place in another State; and a notice that the Warsaw Convention may apply
-- and in most cases limits the liability of carriers.

@ref "Convention, Article 3(1)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      t IS A `Ticket Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ticket contains the particulars Article 3(1) requires` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
            t's `the ticket states the place and date of issue`
        AND t's `the ticket states the places of departure and destination`
        AND t's `the ticket states the agreed stopping places`
        AND t's `the ticket states the name and address of the carrier or carriers`
        AND t's `the ticket states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            t's `the ticket states the places of departure and destination`
        AND (IF t's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State`
             THEN t's `the ticket indicates at least one such stopping place`
             ELSE TRUE)
        AND t's `the ticket contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for death or personal injury and for loss of or damage to baggage`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            t's `the ticket states the places of departure and destination`
        AND (IF t's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State`
             THEN t's `the ticket indicates at least one such stopping place`
             ELSE TRUE)
        AND t's `the ticket contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for death or personal injury and for loss of or damage to baggage`

-- 3(2): the absence, irregularity or loss of the ticket does not affect the existence or
-- validity of the contract, which stays subject to the Convention; but a carrier that accepts
-- a passenger without a ticket (Second Schedule) forfeits every provision excluding or limiting
-- liability, and (First and Third Schedules) a carrier that lets the passenger embark without a
-- ticket, or whose ticket lacks the notice, forfeits Article 22.

@ref "Convention, Article 3(2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      t IS A `Ticket Facts`
GIVETH A Forfeiture
`what the passenger ticket forfeits` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        IF t's `the carrier accepted the passenger, or with the carrier's consent the passenger embarked, without a passenger ticket having been delivered`
        THEN `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        IF     t's `the carrier accepted the passenger, or with the carrier's consent the passenger embarked, without a passenger ticket having been delivered`
            OR (    t's `a passenger ticket was delivered`
                AND NOT t's `the ticket contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for death or personal injury and for loss of or damage to baggage`)
        THEN `Article 22 is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        IF     t's `the carrier accepted the passenger, or with the carrier's consent the passenger embarked, without a passenger ticket having been delivered`
            OR (    t's `a passenger ticket was delivered`
                AND NOT t's `the ticket contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for death or personal injury and for loss of or damage to baggage`)
        THEN `Article 22 is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`

@ref "Convention, Article 3(2)"
`the absence, irregularity or loss of the passenger ticket affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage` MEANS FALSE

-- Article 3(2) (First and Third Schedules): the ticket is prima facie evidence of the
-- conclusion and conditions of the contract.  The Second Schedule has no such sentence.

@ref "Convention, Article 3(2) (First and Third Schedules)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the conclusion and conditions of the contract of carriage` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) does not say that the passenger ticket is prima facie evidence of the contract"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN TRUE

§§ `Section 2, Article 4. Baggage check`

@ref "Convention, Article 4(1) to (3)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      b IS A `Baggage Check Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the baggage check contains the particulars Article 4 requires` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        NOT b's `the baggage is other than small personal objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`
        OR (    b's `a baggage check was delivered`
            AND b's `the baggage check is made out in duplicate, one part for the passenger and one for the carrier`
            AND b's `the check states the place and date of issue`
            AND b's `the check states the places of departure and destination`
            AND b's `the check states the name and address of the carrier or carriers`
            AND b's `the check states the number of the passenger ticket`
            AND b's `the check states that delivery of the baggage will be made to the bearer of the check`
            AND b's `the check states the number and weight of the packages`
            AND b's `the check states the amount of the value declared`
            AND b's `the check states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention`)
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            b's `a baggage check was delivered`
        AND (   b's `the baggage check is combined with or incorporated in a passenger ticket that complies with Article 3`
             OR (    b's `the check states the places of departure and destination`
                 AND (IF b's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State`
                      THEN b's `the check indicates at least one such stopping place`
                      ELSE TRUE)
                 AND b's `the check contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to baggage`))
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            b's `a baggage check was delivered`
        AND (   b's `the baggage check is combined with or incorporated in a passenger ticket that complies with Article 3`
             OR (    b's `the check states the places of departure and destination`
                 AND (IF b's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State`
                      THEN b's `the check indicates at least one such stopping place`
                      ELSE TRUE)
                 AND b's `the check contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to baggage`))

-- 4(4) (Second Schedule): a carrier that accepts baggage without a check, or whose check lacks
-- the ticket number (d), the number and weight of packages (f) or the liability statement (h),
-- forfeits every limiting provision.  4(2) (First and Third Schedules): a carrier that takes
-- charge of baggage without a check, or whose check (unless combined with a compliant ticket)
-- lacks the notice, forfeits Article 22(2).

@ref "Convention, Article 4(4) (Second Schedule) and Article 4(2) (First and Third Schedules)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      b IS A `Baggage Check Facts`
GIVETH A Forfeiture
`what the baggage check forfeits` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        IF     b's `the baggage is other than small personal objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`
           AND (   b's `the carrier took charge of the baggage without a baggage check having been delivered`
                OR (    b's `a baggage check was delivered`
                    AND NOT (    b's `the check states the number of the passenger ticket`
                             AND b's `the check states the number and weight of the packages`
                             AND b's `the check states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention`)))
        THEN `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        IF     b's `the carrier took charge of the baggage without a baggage check having been delivered`
            OR (    NOT b's `the baggage check is combined with or incorporated in a passenger ticket that complies with Article 3`
                AND NOT b's `the check contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to baggage`)
        THEN `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        IF     b's `the carrier took charge of the baggage without a baggage check having been delivered`
            OR (    NOT b's `the baggage check is combined with or incorporated in a passenger ticket that complies with Article 3`
                AND NOT b's `the check contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to baggage`)
        THEN `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`

@ref "Convention, Article 4(4) and 4(2)"
`the absence, irregularity or loss of the baggage check affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Section 3, Articles 5 to 9. Air waybill (Second Schedule and First Schedule) and documentation relating to cargo (Third Schedule)`

-- 5(1) (Second and First): every carrier of cargo may require the consignor to make out an air
-- waybill and every consignor may require the carrier to accept it.  The Third Schedule says
-- instead that an air waybill shall be delivered (5(1)), that another means preserving a
-- record may be substituted with the consignor's consent (5(2)), and that the impossibility of
-- using it at transit or destination does not entitle the carrier to refuse the cargo (5(3)).

@ref "Convention, Article 5(1)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier may require an air waybill and the consignor may require the carrier to accept it` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention (Third Schedule) provides that an air waybill shall be delivered (Article 5(1)); it does not give the carrier a right to require one or the consignor a right to require the carrier to accept it"

@ref "Convention, Article 5(2) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      w IS A `Waybill Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `another means of preserving the record may be substituted for an air waybill` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no provision for substituting another means of preserving the record for an air waybill"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention (First Schedule) has no provision for substituting another means of preserving the record for an air waybill"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
        w's `another means that preserves a record of the carriage was substituted, with the consignor's consent, for an air waybill`

@ref "Convention, Article 5(3) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the impossibility of using another means at transit or destination entitles the carrier to refuse the cargo` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no provision about the impossibility of using another means of preserving the record"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention (First Schedule) has no provision about the impossibility of using another means of preserving the record"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN FALSE

@ref "Convention, Article 5(2) (Second and First Schedules) and Article 9 (Third Schedule)"
`the absence, irregularity or loss of the air waybill affects the existence or the validity of the contract of carriage` MEANS FALSE

-- 6: the air waybill is made out in three original parts; the first marked "for the carrier"
-- and signed by the consignor; the second marked "for the consignee" and signed by the
-- consignor and the carrier; the third signed by the carrier and handed to the consignor after
-- the cargo has been accepted.  The carrier signs on acceptance of the cargo (Second Schedule)
-- or before loading (First Schedule); the Third Schedule states no time for the carrier's
-- signature.

@ref "Convention, Article 6(1) to (3)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      w IS A `Waybill Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the air waybill complies with Article 6` IF
        w's `the air waybill was made out in three original parts`
    AND w's `the first part is marked "for the carrier" and signed by the consignor`
    AND w's `the second part is marked "for the consignee" and signed by the consignor and the carrier`
    AND w's `the third part is signed by the carrier and handed to the consignor after the cargo has been accepted`
    AND (CONSIDER c
         WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN w's `the carrier signed on acceptance of the cargo`
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN w's `the carrier signed before the cargo was loaded on board the aircraft`
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN TRUE)

@ref "Convention, Article 6(5) (Second and First Schedules) and Article 6(4) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN `the carrier made out the air waybill at the request of the consignor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is proof to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is deemed to have made out the air waybill on behalf of the consignor` IF
        `the carrier made out the air waybill at the request of the consignor`
    AND NOT `there is proof to the contrary`

-- 7: the carrier may require separate air waybills where there is more than one package; the
-- Third Schedule adds that the consignor may require separate receipts where the other means
-- are used.

@ref "Convention, Article 7"
GIVEN `there is more than one package` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier may require the consignor to make out separate air waybills` IF
    `there is more than one package`

@ref "Convention, Article 7(b) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      `there is more than one package` IS A BOOLEAN
      w IS A `Waybill Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignor may require the carrier to deliver separate receipts` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no provision for separate receipts"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention (First Schedule) has no provision for separate receipts"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            `there is more than one package`
        AND w's `another means that preserves a record of the carriage was substituted, with the consignor's consent, for an air waybill`

-- 8: the contents of the air waybill.  Second Schedule: seventeen particulars, (a) to (q).
-- First Schedule: places of departure and destination; an indication of a stopping place where
-- both places are in one High Contracting Party's territory with an agreed stopping place in
-- another State; the notice to the consignor.  Third Schedule: the same first two, and the
-- weight of the consignment.

@ref "Convention, Article 8"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      w IS A `Waybill Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the air waybill contains the particulars Article 8 requires` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
            w's `the waybill states the place and date of its execution`
        AND w's `the waybill states the places of departure and destination`
        AND w's `the waybill states the agreed stopping places`
        AND w's `the waybill states the name and address of the consignor`
        AND w's `the waybill states the name and address of the first carrier`
        AND w's `the waybill states the name and address of the consignee, if the case so requires`
        AND w's `the waybill states the nature of the cargo`
        AND w's `the waybill states the number of the packages, the method of packing and the particular marks or numbers`
        AND w's `the waybill states the weight, the quantity and the volume or dimensions of the cargo`
        AND w's `the waybill states the apparent condition of the cargo and of the packing`
        AND w's `the waybill states the freight if agreed, the date and place of payment and who is to pay`
        AND w's `the waybill states, if the cargo is sent for payment on delivery, the price and any expenses`
        AND w's `the waybill states the amount of the value declared`
        AND w's `the waybill states the number of parts`
        AND w's `the waybill states the documents handed to the carrier to accompany it`
        AND w's `the waybill states the time fixed for completion and a brief note of the route, if agreed`
        AND w's `the waybill states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
            w's `the waybill states the places of departure and destination`
        AND (IF w's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State`
             THEN w's `the waybill indicates at least one such stopping place`
             ELSE TRUE)
        AND w's `the waybill contains the notice to the consignor that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to cargo`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            w's `the waybill states the places of departure and destination`
        AND (IF w's `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State`
             THEN w's `the waybill indicates at least one such stopping place`
             ELSE TRUE)
        AND w's `the waybill or the receipt indicates the weight of the consignment`

-- 9: the effect of a defective or missing air waybill.  Second Schedule: a carrier that
-- accepts cargo without an air waybill, or whose waybill lacks any of the particulars (a) to
-- (i) and (q), forfeits every limiting provision.  First Schedule: a carrier that loads cargo
-- with consent without an air waybill, or whose waybill lacks the Article 8(c) notice,
-- forfeits Article 22(2).  Third Schedule: non-compliance with Articles 5 to 8 does not affect
-- the contract, which stays subject to the Convention including the limits.

@ref "Convention, Article 9"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      w IS A `Waybill Facts`
GIVETH A Forfeiture
`what the air waybill forfeits` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
        IF     w's `the carrier accepted the cargo, or with the carrier's consent it was loaded on board the aircraft, without an air waybill having been made out`
            OR (    w's `an air waybill was made out`
                AND NOT (    w's `the waybill states the place and date of its execution`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the places of departure and destination`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the agreed stopping places`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the name and address of the consignor`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the name and address of the first carrier`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the name and address of the consignee, if the case so requires`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the nature of the cargo`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the number of the packages, the method of packing and the particular marks or numbers`
                         AND w's `the waybill states the weight, the quantity and the volume or dimensions of the cargo`
                         AND w's `the waybill states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention`))
        THEN `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
        IF     w's `the carrier accepted the cargo, or with the carrier's consent it was loaded on board the aircraft, without an air waybill having been made out`
            OR (    w's `an air waybill was made out`
                AND NOT w's `the waybill contains the notice to the consignor that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to cargo`)
        THEN `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
        ELSE `nothing is forfeited`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN `nothing is forfeited`

§§ `Articles 10 to 11. The consignor's responsibility; evidence`

-- 10(2): Second Schedule: the consignor is liable for all damage suffered by the carrier or any
-- other person by reason of the irregularity, incorrectness or incompleteness of the
-- particulars and statements.  First and Third Schedules: the consignor indemnifies the carrier
-- against all damage suffered by him or by any other person to whom the carrier is liable.
-- 10(3) (Third Schedule): the carrier indemnifies the consignor for the particulars the
-- carrier inserts.

@ref "Convention, Article 10(2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      i IS AN `Indemnity Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignor is liable for the damage` IF
        i's `the damage is by reason of the irregularity, incorrectness or incompleteness of the particulars and statements furnished by the consignor or on his behalf`
    AND (CONSIDER c
         WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN
                i's `the damage is suffered by the carrier`
             OR i's `the damage is suffered by another person`
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN
                i's `the damage is suffered by the carrier`
             OR (    i's `the damage is suffered by another person`
                 AND i's `the carrier is liable to that other person`)
         WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
                i's `the damage is suffered by the carrier`
             OR (    i's `the damage is suffered by another person`
                 AND i's `the carrier is liable to that other person`))

@ref "Convention, Article 10(3) (Third Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      i IS AN `Indemnity Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier must indemnify the consignor` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) has no provision that the carrier indemnifies the consignor"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) Convention (First Schedule) has no provision that the carrier indemnifies the consignor"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
            i's `the damage is suffered by the consignor or by a person to whom the consignor is liable`
        AND i's `the damage is by reason of the irregularity, incorrectness or incompleteness of the particulars and statements inserted by the carrier or on his behalf in the receipt or record`

-- 10(1): the consignor is responsible for the correctness of the particulars he inserts: a
-- statement of responsibility whose consequence is 10(2), so inert.

@ref "Convention, Article 11(1)"
`the air waybill or the receipt for the cargo is prima facie evidence of the conclusion of the contract, of the receipt or acceptance of the cargo and of the conditions of carriage` MEANS TRUE

@ref "Convention, Article 11(2)"
GIVEN s IS A `Statement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is evidence against the carrier` IF
    CONSIDER s's `kind of statement`
    WHEN `a statement of the weight, dimensions or packing of the cargo, or the number of packages` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statement of the quantity, volume or condition of the cargo` THEN
           s's `the statement was checked by the carrier in the presence of the consignor and is stated in the waybill to have been`
        OR s's `the statement relates to the apparent condition of the cargo`

§§ `Articles 12 to 16. Disposition of cargo; delivery; customs`

-- 12(1) and (4): the consignor may dispose of the cargo; the right ceases when the
-- consignee's right begins under Article 13, and resumes if the consignee declines to accept or
-- cannot be communicated with.

@ref "Convention, Article 12(1) and (4)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disposition Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignor has the right of disposition` IF
        NOT d's `the consignee's right under Article 13 has begun`
     OR d's `the consignee declines to accept the air waybill or the cargo`
     OR d's `the consignee cannot be communicated with`

@ref "Convention, Article 12(3)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disposition Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable for the damage caused by obeying the consignor's orders` IF
        d's `the carrier obeyed the consignor's orders without requiring production of the part of the air waybill or the receipt delivered to the consignor`
    AND d's `damage has been caused to a person lawfully in possession of that part`

-- 12(2): if it is impossible to carry out the consignor's orders the carrier must inform him
-- forthwith.  The text states no number of days.

@ref "Convention, Article 12(2)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the Convention` `Act under the Convention`
`the carrier's duty to inform the consignor that his orders cannot be carried out` MEANS
    PARTY `The carrier`
    MUST `inform the consignor of the impossibility of carrying out his orders`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The carrier` BECAUSE "the consignor was not informed forthwith that it was impossible to carry out his orders, as Article 12(2) requires"

@ref "Convention, Article 13(1)"
GIVEN `the cargo has arrived at the place of destination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consignor has exercised his right of disposition under Article 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charges due have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of carriage have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignee is entitled to require delivery of the cargo` IF
        `the cargo has arrived at the place of destination`
    AND NOT `the consignor has exercised his right of disposition under Article 12`
    AND `the charges due have been paid`
    AND `the conditions of carriage have been complied with`

@ref "Convention, Article 13(2)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to the Convention` `Act under the Convention`
`the carrier's duty to give the consignee notice of the arrival of the cargo` MEANS
    PARTY `The carrier`
    MUST `give notice to the consignee of the arrival of the cargo`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The carrier` BECAUSE "the consignee was not given notice as soon as the cargo arrived, as Article 13(2) requires unless otherwise agreed"

-- 13(3): the consignee may enforce the rights flowing from the contract if the carrier admits
-- loss of the cargo, or the cargo has not arrived at the expiration of seven days after the
-- date it ought to have arrived (NOTES.md fork F5).

@ref "Convention, Article 13(3)"
GIVEN d IS A `Delivery Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignee may enforce the rights which flow from the contract of carriage` IF
        d's `the carrier admits the loss of the cargo`
     OR (    NOT d's `the cargo has arrived`
         AND d's `the date on which the rights are asserted` GREATER THAN d's `the date the cargo ought to have arrived` PLUS 7)

@ref "Convention, Article 14"
GIVEN `the person carries out the obligations imposed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignor or the consignee may enforce in his own name the rights given by Articles 12 and 13` IF
    `the person carries out the obligations imposed by the contract`

-- 15(1): Articles 12 to 14 do not affect the relations of consignor and consignee with each
-- other or the mutual relations of third parties: a saving, inert.  15(2): they can be varied
-- only by express provision in the air waybill (First and Second Schedules) or the air
-- waybill or the receipt for the cargo (Third Schedule).

@ref "Convention, Article 15(2)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
      `the variation is an express provision in the air waybill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation is an express provision in the receipt for the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Articles 12, 13 and 14 have been validly varied` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN `the variation is an express provision in the air waybill`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN `the variation is an express provision in the air waybill`
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN
           `the variation is an express provision in the air waybill`
        OR `the variation is an express provision in the receipt for the cargo`

@ref "Convention, Article 15(3) (First Schedule)"
GIVEN c IS A Convention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `nothing in the Convention prevents the issue of a negotiable air waybill` IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the Warsaw Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw Convention (Second Schedule) says nothing about a negotiable air waybill"
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` THEN REFUSE "the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention (Third Schedule) has no Article 15(3) about a negotiable air waybill"

@ref "Convention, Article 16(1)"
GIVEN k IS A `Customs Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignor is liable to the carrier for the damage occasioned by the customs information or documents` IF
        NOT k's `the consignor furnished the information and documents necessary to meet the formalities of customs, octroi or police`
    AND k's `the carrier has suffered damage occasioned by their absence, insufficiency or irregularity`
    AND NOT k's `the damage is due to the fault of the carrier or his servants or agents`

@ref "Convention, Article 16(2)"
`the carrier is under an obligation to enquire into the correctness or sufficiency of the customs information or documents` MEANS FALSE
